## Week 1: Jan 1 – Jan 4 (Research & Planning)

| Date | Day | Hours | Work Done |
|------|-----|-------|-----------|
| Jan 1 | Wed | 8 | Received project brief from supervisor — build an AI-powered body scanning platform that captures body measurements from photos and provides fashion intelligence. Studied the core requirements and understood the overall vision. Set up development environment (Node.js, Python, PostgreSQL, VS Code). |
| Jan 2 | Thu | 8 | Researched **body measurement extraction** from images. Studied computer vision approaches — MediaPipe pose estimation, SMPL body model fitting (Skinned Multi-Person Linear Model). Explored Three.js for 3D body model visualization in the browser. Studied existing platforms like BodyBlock and 3DBODY.TECH for feature inspiration. |
| Jan 3 | Fri | 8 | Researched remaining features — **clothing fit analysis** (garment vs body comparison, material stretch factors), **wardrobe analytics** (composition tracking, color analysis), **trend intelligence** (AI-driven fashion trend tracking), **Razorpay payment integration** for subscriptions. Studied competitor pricing models. |
| Jan 4 | Sat | 8 | Created a **detailed implementation plan** listing 7 core features: (1) Body Scan & Measurement, (2) Saved Measurements, (3) Fashion IQ Score, (4) Body Tracker, (5) Wardrobe Analytics, (6) Trend Analysis, (7) Clothing Fit Checker. Plus supporting pages (Home, Auth, Profile, Pricing, Features Showcase). Designed database schema and API endpoint structure. Chose tech stack — React + TypeScript, FastAPI, PostgreSQL. |

